  "summary": "The paper studies four gate-based QAOA variants—QAOA, WSQAOA, WS-Init-QAOA, and RQAOA—on five QUBO-encoded NP-complete problems using ideal and noisy circuit simulations. It reports 100 random instances per problem size, 5-19 qubits in ideal runs, up to 10 qubits in noisy runs, 1-7 layers ideal and 1-4 noisy, and finds model RMSE below 0.09 on the baseline test set and below 0.07 on the extrapolation set. No practical quantum advantage is demonstrated; the contribution is a design-automation and prediction framework.",
